   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif;color:#0b5394\">Jamile, </div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif;color:#0b5394\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif;color:#0b5394\">the shapes at the tips of the trajectories correspond to group means. You can use a combination of coord.subset to divide your groups, then mshape on each group, and then plotRefToTarget to depict the specific shape changes across your vectors.</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif;color:#0b5394\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif;color:#0b5394\">Hope this helps</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif;color:#0b5394\">Antigoni</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
