    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&quot;trebuchet ms&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">J</span><span class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&quot;trebuchet ms&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(11,83,148)\">amile, I just realised I was not fully clear: obviously, what you see in the trajectory analysis scatterplots is a simplified view, i.e. a projection of group means to the PC1-PC2 space. The solution I´m proposing, would provide a visualization of the &quot;real&quot; (i.e. full-shape) vector between points, which is the one being statistically analysed.</span></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
